WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.975
The example is two Python files, one
sample workflow and two test files.

2
00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:08.413
The workflow has two jobs with
a deliberate wall between them.

3
00:00:08.413 --> 00:00:13.350
The first can read the tenant: it signs
in, gets a Graph token for the right host,

4
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:18.837
runs the validation kit, compares with the
previous package and writes new evidence.

5
00:00:18.837 --> 00:00:23.262
The second can write to the issue
tracker, but has no Azure access at all.

6
00:00:23.262 --> 00:00:27.050
So the identity that reads the
tenant never writes to the tracker.

7
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:32.640
One check is delegated only, so it's
honestly listed as unverified on every run.
